From: quiet-pixel-987 <quiet.pixel.987667@local.dev>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 18:41:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 600/613] Add encrypted Coves: password-shared,
 quantum-resistant file vaults

A cove is an AES-256-GCM vault committed at .forkmesh/coves/<slug>.cove and
versioned by git. A team shares one password out-of-band; entered in repo or
global Settings it unlocks matching coves, which show locked/greyed in the file
tree until unlocked (auto-show optional). Opening a cove logs it locally and, if
the creator opted in, sends a best-effort signed "opened" alert back to the
creator's node over the relay.

- CoveCrypto/CoveStore: per-cove salt + PBKDF2; documents + access log payload
- ChatBackend/ServerNode: ephemeral signed cove-open broadcast + coveOpened signal
- MainWindowCoves.cpp: viewer, settings UI, unlock/auto-show, onCoveOpened
- Tests: crypto round-trip, wrong-password rejection, store round-trip

Note: bundles concurrent in-progress MainWindow.cpp changes present in the tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
